  "title": "Greenland Drilling Plans Delayed Amid U.S. Government Concerns",
  "summary": "A U.S. oil company has delayed its plans to drill in Greenland due to government warnings and concerns about environmental impacts, with locals expressing opposition.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The U.S. oil company Greenland Energy Co. and its partner 80 Mile have delayed planned oil drilling in Greenland until winter 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The delay is due to government warnings about environmental and energy risks, and local opposition.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The drilling plans are set to take effect in 2027.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
